# =====================================================================
# 25. IMPORTANT KUBERNETES CONCEPTS LEARNED
# =====================================================================
#
# Docker:
#   Packages each application into a container image.
#
# Kind:
#   Creates local Kubernetes clusters using Docker containers.
#
# Kubernetes Node:
#   Machine that runs Kubernetes workloads.
#
# Pod:
#   Smallest deployable unit in Kubernetes.
#
# Deployment:
#   Maintains replicas and performs rolling updates.
#
# Replica:
#   Additional application instance for availability and scaling.
#
# ClusterIP Service:
#   Provides stable internal access and distributes requests.
#
# EndpointSlice:
#   Tracks backend Pod addresses used by Services.
#
# Namespace:
#   Organizes Kubernetes resources logically.
#
# NGINX Ingress Controller:
#   Implements HTTP routing rules for incoming traffic.
#
# Ingress Resource:
#   Defines which URL path maps to which Kubernetes Service.
#
# Helm:
#   Installs and manages packaged Kubernetes applications.
#
# Port Forwarding:
#   Creates a temporary local connection to a Kubernetes workload.
#
# Rolling Update:
#   Gradually replaces application Pods with a new version.
#
# Scaling:
#   Changes the number of application replicas.
#
# Troubleshooting:
#   Uses kubectl logs, describe, events, curl, and network checks.
